# Survivors-Udemy Project Structure

## Folder Layout

| Folder | Purpose |
|--------|---------|
| `scenes/game_object/` | Player, enemies (basic_enemy, bat_enemy, ghost_enemy, wizard_enemy, spider_enemy, ogre_enemy), experience_vial |
| `scenes/ability/` | Per-ability: `*_ability/` (visual/projectile), `*_ability_controller/` (logic) |
| `scenes/component/` | Reusable components: HurtboxComponent, VelocityComponent, HealthComponent, DeathComponent, HitboxComponent, VialDropComponent |
| `scenes/manager/` | UpgradeManager, EnemyManager, ArenaTimeManager, ExperienceManager |
| `scenes/UI/` | Main menu, ability selector, upgrade screen, end screen, pause menu, highscores |
| `scenes/autoload/` | GameEvents, StartingAbilityRegistry, HighscoresManager, ScreenTransition, etc. |
| `resources/upgrades/` | Ability resource `.tres` files: `*_path.tres`, `*.tres`, `*_lv2.tres` … `*_lv9.tres` |
| `resources/effects/`  | Hit spark configs, Planck fire temperature gradient EXR(s) (e.g. from plancks-law-colors), `fire_temperature_gradient.tres` |

## Game Flow

```
Main Menu (main_menu.tscn) [run scene]
  Play → Ability Selector → Start → Main (main.tscn)
  Player dies → End Screen → Restart or Main Menu
```

## Key Systems

- **UpgradeManager** (`scenes/manager/upgrade_manager.gd`): Upgrade pool, ability levels, applies starting ability controller into player `Abilities` node
- **StartingAbilityRegistry** (autoload): Unlocked abilities, selected starting ability, `get_selectable_ability_paths()` (excludes smite)
- **GameEvents** (autoload): `experience_vial_collected`, `ability_upgrade_added`, `player_damaged`
- **HighscoresManager** (autoload): Top 5 scores, `user://highscores.dat`

## Ability Architecture

- **Resources**: `AbilityUpgradePath` → `Ability` (level 1) + `AbilityUpgrade` (lv2–9)
- **Scenes**: `Ability.ability_controller_scene` → controller under player `Abilities` node
- **Controller pattern**: `_apply_stats_from_level()`, `_apply_attack_speed()`, listen to `GameEvents.ability_upgrade_added` for live updates

## Enemy Structure

- **Base**: `Area2D` in group `"enemy"`
- **Components**: HurtboxComponent, VelocityComponent, HealthComponent, DeathComponent, VialDropComponent, HitFlashComponent
- **Pattern**: `velocity_component.accelerate_to_player()` + `move()` in `_process`; Hurtbox receives damage from HitboxComponent

## Naming Conventions

- Scenes/scripts: `snake_case.tscn`, `snake_case.gd`
- Ability folders: `*_ability/`, `*_ability_controller/`
- Resources: `ability_id.tres`, `ability_id_path.tres`
- Unique nodes: `%NodeName` for `$%NodeName` access

## Ability Creation (Summary)

When adding a new ability, touch these areas:

- **Resources**: `resources/upgrades/{id}.tres` (Ability), `{id}_lv2.tres` … `{id}_lv9.tres`, `{id}_path.tres` (AbilityUpgradePath)
- **Manager**: Register path in `upgrade_manager.gd` (`_ability_paths`, `ability_levels[id] = 0` or `1` for pre-attached)
- **Controller**: `scenes/ability/{id}_ability_controller/` — Node + Timer, script with `_apply_stats_from_level()`, `_apply_attack_speed()`, `on_timer_timeout`, `on_ability_upgrade_added`
- **Visual**: `scenes/ability/{id}_ability/` — Node2D with either HitboxComponent (hitbox-based) or no hitbox (direct-damage)
- **Wire**: Base Ability `.tres` → `ability_controller_scene` = controller scene

**Groups used by controllers**: `"player"`, `"enemy"`, `"foreground_layer"`, `"upgrade_manager"`.

## Ability Damage Models

- **Hitbox-based (Sword, Axe, Ball Lightning)**: Visual scene has HitboxComponent. Controller sets `hitbox_component.damage` (and any spawn params), adds visual to `foreground_layer`. Enemies' HurtboxComponent overlaps hitbox; damage can be applied in controller (one shot) or in visual script (e.g. tick-based overlap checks + `hurtbox.apply_damage()`).
- **Direct-damage (Chain Lightning, Bite)**: No hitbox on visual. Controller finds targets, calls `hurtbox.apply_damage(...)` on each, then spawns visual (e.g. chain positions, or one visual per target with `impact` signal for timing).

## Controller Pattern (Required)

- `_get_upgrade_manager()` → `get_tree().get_first_node_in_group("upgrade_manager")`
- `_get_*_level()` or `_get_ability_level()` → `manager.get_ability_level("ability_id")`
- `_apply_stats_from_level()`: map levels 1–9 to `base_wait_time`, `_damage_flat_bonus`, `_rate_reduction`, quantity, and any ability-specific stats
- `_ready()`: connect Timer timeout, `GameEvents.ability_upgrade_added`, call `_apply_stats_from_level()` and `_apply_attack_speed()`
- `_apply_attack_speed()`: apply `player.attack_speed_multiplier` and rate reductions to `$Timer.wait_time`, clamp with `MIN_WAIT_TIME`
- `on_ability_upgrade_added`: if `upgrade.ability_id == "ability_id"` → refresh stats and attack speed; also handle `generic_attack_speed`, `generic_damage`, `generic_size`, `generic_duration` (often no-op, read from player at attack time)
- Damage formula: `(base_damage + _damage_flat_bonus + flat_bonus) * damage_mult` (read `player.damage_multiplier`, `player.damage_flat_bonus` at attack time); apply `size_mult` / `duration_mult` from player when spawning visuals

## Collision (Abilities)

- **HitboxComponent**: `collision_layer = 4`, `collision_mask = 0`
- **HurtboxComponent** (on enemies): `collision_mask` includes 4 to receive hitbox overlaps

